    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling lineup led by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, our strongest play with a 72.16 score. Facing Andre Pallante, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a favorable 4.17 xERA matchup and a significant 14% dynamic platoon boost, solidifying his role in the #3 hole. Close behind is **Jacob Wilson** (66.56), who leverages a plus-matchup against Rhett Lowder; his 18% SP skill adjustment highlights the advantage of exploiting Lowder\u2019s susceptibility to contact. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (65.50) and **Kyle Tucker** (63.19) remain elite, high-floor anchors, though **Kyle Tucker** must contend with a tougher draw against Shota Imanaga, who continues to suppress run production despite the park factor.\n\nWe face a difficult bench decision regarding **Gunnar Henderson**, whose 54.45 score narrowly missed the cut. Despite his raw talent, the combination of a sharp opposing arm in Reid Detmers and a -15% platoon penalty against the left-handed starter pushed **Gunnar Henderson** to the pine in favor of the higher-efficiency projections for **Nasim Nunez** and **Denzer Guzman**. While **Nasim Nunez** carries a negative adjustment for his spot in the lineup, his role in the stolen base hierarchy remains vital for our 5x5 strategy. We are also monitoring 35% rain risks for both **Denzer Guzman** and **Gunnar Henderson**, as well as a 33% threat impacting **Drake Baldwin**; should those games face delays, we may need to pivot to bench assets like **Miguel Vargas** or **Jorge Polanco** to ensure we hit our daily game caps efficiently.",
